Vendored from gh-pages at eacdef4. It includes w3c/data-shapes commit
004346d (2026-11-19), which renames NOT DATA to NOT GROUND and WHERE DATA to
WHERE GROUND, and the GROUP aggregate tests of pull requests #1347, #1375 and
#1380.
Do not edit by hand.

Note on the language: `FOR ?var IN <shape>`, and the `IF … THEN` rule form,
were removed from the SRL grammar upstream on 2026-08-24 (commits 58fdfc6 and
cfbcd3c), and the five tests that covered them went with them. There is one
rule production left: RULE iri? HeadTemplate 'WHERE' 'GROUND'? BodyPattern.

